// GOLDEN VECTORS for the CSS selector tester
// (set "css-selector-tester-golden-2026-10-05").
//
// Each vector is an HTML document and a list of selectors; the pinned value is
// the whole result: the element rows (with path, line and the selectors that
// match each), each selector's validity, matches, count, specificity,
// pseudo-element and notes. The matcher's answers for these documents were
// compared with Chromium's querySelectorAll (139 of 146 selectors agree; the
// seven that differ are of five kinds, each deliberate: the s flag and the
// quoted :lang() form, which Level 4 defines and the browser does not yet
// accept; :optional on a hidden input, where the HTML Standard and Chromium
// differ; :valid, which this tester does not evaluate; and the three
// pseudo-element selectors, for which querySelectorAll returns nothing by
// design while the tester lists the originating elements).
//
// Expected values were captured from compute.run() on 2026-10-05.
// ============================================================================

